ie"]]}]},"ingredient/chervil":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/chervil","n":"Chervil","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Chervil, sometimes called French parsley or garden chervil (to distinguish it from similar plants also called chervil), is a delicate annual herb related to parsley. It was formerly called myrhis due to its volatile oil with an aroma similar to the resinous substance myrrh. It is commonly used to season mild-flavoured dishes and is a constituent of the French herb mixture fines herbes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chervil"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chervil"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Cali-Mex cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence",[["Green goddess dressing","dish/green-goddess-dressing"]]],["Cuisine of California","cuisine/cuisine-of-california",[["Green goddess dressing","dish/green-goddess-dressing"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Chives","ingredient/chives"],["Lemon","ingredient/lemon"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Sour cream","ingredient/sour-cream"],["Tarragon","ingredient/tarragon"]]}]},"dish/jjamppong":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/jjamppong","n":"Jjamppong","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Korean Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Jjamppong is a Chinese-style Korean noodle soup with red, spicy seafood- or pork-based broth flavored with gochugaru (chili powder). Common ingredients include onions, garlic, Korean zucchini, carrots, cabbages, squid, mussels, and pork. The dish was inspired by Chinese cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-jjamppong"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jjamppong"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Korean Chinese cuisi